src/pipeline/server.py:750:     def _run_semantic_pipeline(content, manifest, step_contexts, per_step, note):
src/pipeline/server.py:751:         """Shared by the real-capture flow (_apply_transcript) and the photo
src/pipeline/server.py:752:         build flow (_generate_photo): when the deterministic placement
src/pipeline/server.py:753:         (transcript.py) collapses onto a single step despite there being
src/pipeline/server.py:754:         multiple real steps -- its own loud WARNING signature -- this tries
src/pipeline/server.py:755:         the semantic LLM pipeline instead: stage 1 (semantic_align) picks
src/pipeline/server.py:756:         verbatim split points from the full transcript + step contexts;
src/pipeline/server.py:757:         stage 2 (polish_narration) then rewrites each resulting segment for
src/pipeline/server.py:758:         readability, gated so nothing invented or dropped is ever trusted
src/pipeline/server.py:759:         silently. Either stage failing just falls back to what came before
src/pipeline/server.py:760:         it -- semantic_align failing keeps the original single-block
src/pipeline/server.py:761:         deterministic result (with its warning); polish_narration failing
src/pipeline/server.py:762:         keeps stage 1's verbatim placement. Returns (per_step, note,
src/pipeline/server.py:763:         placement_meta) -- placement_meta is None if semantic_align declined
src/pipeline/server.py:764:         or "WARNING" wasn't in `note` to begin with (nothing to try)."""
src/pipeline/server.py:765:         if "WARNING" not in note:
src/pipeline/server.py:766:             return per_step, note, None
src/pipeline/server.py:767: 
src/pipeline/server.py:768:         placement_meta = None
src/pipeline/server.py:769:         narrative_llm = make_narrative_llm_client()
