src/pipeline/polish.py:209:     a field-level pass has no per-step [verify] blockquote to attach one to
src/pipeline/polish.py:210:     for `narrative_text` (which isn't step-scoped), so a dropped clause here
src/pipeline/polish.py:211:     is just a hard reject. `original`/`rewrite` are a single field's text --
src/pipeline/polish.py:212:     the whole document (`generate_polish_pass`, via `_gate` below), a step's
src/pipeline/polish.py:213:     `"text"`, a step's `"narration"`, or `narrative_text`
src/pipeline/polish.py:214:     (`generate_polish_fields`) -- the checks themselves don't care which.
src/pipeline/polish.py:215: 
src/pipeline/polish.py:216:     Uses `degenerate_shape_reason` rather than `degenerate_reason` -- the
src/pipeline/polish.py:217:     latter's absolute `_LENGTH_CAP` (600 chars) is sized for short per-step
src/pipeline/polish.py:218:     captions/narration segments and would reject any real multi-step
src/pipeline/polish.py:219:     document or narrative outright. Document-scale length sanity is instead
src/pipeline/polish.py:220:     covered by check 3 below (length ratio against the original)."""
