      "title": "Coordinate regression coverage omits mixed DPI and negative monitor origins",
      "file": "tests/test_recorder.py",
      "line": 155,
      "evidence": "The monitor-local regression uses `{\"left\": 1920, \"top\": 0, \"width\": 1920, \"height\": 1080}`. recorder.py:143 correctly subtracts origin, and :149-152 translates element bounds. `rg -n 'DPI|dpi|SetProcess|SetThread' src tests scripts` produced no matches; sopforge.spec:29 specifies runtime_hooks=[]. No test establishes physical-coordinate agreement under mixed scaling. Dependency-provided DPI awareness remains unverified.",
      "command": "rg -n 'DPI|dpi|SetProcess|SetThread' src tests scripts",
